  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tajikistan: Improved Prosecution of Trafficking in Persons and Victim Support Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to an improved national response to trafficking in persons, including internal trafficking, in Tajikistan. The project was designed in response to the 2020 TIP Report recommendations for Tajikistan. In direct cooperation with the Government of Tajikistan, IOM expects to achieve the following outcomes. Outcome 1: Improved performance of the state institutions on the prosecution of internal/international TIP cases and advancement of the legal framework. Outcome 2: Law Enforcement Agencies apply victim-centered, trauma-informed and survivor informed approaches during TIP investigation and prosecution. Outcome 3: Information from awareness raising and outreach initiatives reach the most at-risk groups and is used by communities to refer potential trafficking cases to the service providers.</narrative>
  </description>
